R"DATA(
# apk-tools/test/solver/, ported by tools/mkfixtures.py. A .repo or
# .installed is verbatim but for two re-spellings: C: is restamped from
# apk's Q1 to the Q2 §1.1 defines, hashing the old value so that equal
# stays equal and distinct stays distinct; and a repeated D:, p: or i:,
# which apk
# accumulates and Package_Format.md §1 calls malformed: the lines are
# folded into the one space-separated list §6 defines, which is the same
# thing said the way this grammar says it. A .test has @EXPECT reduced to
# the actions apk chose and the order it chose them in, the `(N/M)`
# counter and the `OK:` line being its printer's rather than its
# solver's.
#
# 72 of 119 cases. The 47 dropped, each needing something the solver
# is not:
#
#   15  repository pinning
#       pinning1 pinning2 pinning3 pinning4 pinning5 pinning6 pinning7 pinning8 pinning9 pinning10 pinning11 pinning12 pinning13 pinning14 pinning15
#    8  apk upgrading itself
#       selfupgrade1 selfupgrade2 selfupgrade3 selfupgrade4 selfupgrade5 selfupgrade6 selfupgrade7 selfupgrade8
#    6  the `fix` applet
#       fix1 fix2 fix3 fix4 fix5 fix6
#    4  -t .virtual, a package built on the command line
#       basic8 basic9 error6 error7
#    3  --no-network or a cache index: availability masking
#       basic7 basic12 basic16
#    3  -v: the verbose summary and the no-longer-available note
#       basic20 installif11 installif12
#    3  world dependency spelling, rejected before the solver
#       error8 error9 error10
#    2  --force-broken-world
#       basic10 basic11
#    1  arch
#       basic19
#    1  an index dependency carrying @tag
#       error11
#    1  `apk del`'s not-removed report
#       provides-prio3

